course: dictionary
lesson: 13947
title: Lhasa, a city on the roof of the world
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Lhasa is a name, so it starts with a capital letter. It is a proper noun: the name of one special place. «We flew to Lhasa to see the Himalayan mountains.» The word city tells you that Lhasa is a place, and mountains tell you where it is.
explain: Lhasa is very high up, about 3,650 metres above sea level. «Mia felt dizzy when she first walked up the steps in Lhasa.» That height is one reason Lhasa is one of the highest cities in the world. Try the word «high» in place of Lhasa in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Lhasa is also a holy city for Tibetan Buddhists. «Pilgrims walked slowly around the holy city, praying as they went.» Pilgrims are people who travel to a holy place, so the clues are pilgrims and praying. The Potala Palace in Lhasa was the home of the Dalai Lama.
fact: Lhasa is a proper noun, so it always starts with a capital letter.
fact: «Lhasa» means the main city of Tibet, high in the Himalayas, now under China's rule.
fact: Lhasa is one of the highest cities in the world, about 3,650 metres up.
fact: The Potala Palace in Lhasa was the home of the Dalai Lama.
fact: A Lhasa Apso is a small, long-haired dog breed from Tibet.
exercise: «Lhasa is a city high in the Himalayas.» Where is Lhasa? | In Australia | In Scotland | *In Tibet | In London
exercise: «Our dog is a Lhasa Apso, with long silky hair.» What kind of thing is a Lhasa Apso? | A holy palace | A mountain | A city | *A small dog breed
exercise: Why does Lhasa start with a capital letter? | *Because it is a proper noun, the name of one special place | Because it is a dog's name | Because it starts every sentence | Because it is a very big city
test: «Pilgrims travel to Lhasa to pray in a holy city.» What does holy mean in this sentence? | Very cold | *Special to a religion and sacred | Full of noise | Under the sea
test: «The city is about 3,650 metres high.» What does this tell you about Lhasa? | It is smaller than a village | *It is one of the highest cities in the world | It is under the sea | It is very flat
exam: «Mia's dog is a Lhasa Apso from Tibet.» Which is true? | *A Lhasa Apso is a small, long-haired dog breed | Tibet is a dog breed | Lhasa Apso is a city in Tibet | Lhasa is only a palace
